### LC 621 — Task Scheduler

---

### Brute Force — Simulation Approach

**Idea:**
Simulate the CPU scheduler interval by interval. At each interval, pick the most frequent available task. If no task is available, CPU sits idle.

**Data Structures:**
- HashMap — count frequency of each task
- Max Heap — always gives most frequent available task
- Cooldown Queue — holds tasks waiting for cooldown to expire. Each entry stores `[remainingCount, releaseTime]`

**Step by step:**
- Build frequency map from tasks array
- Put all frequencies into Max Heap
- At each interval:
  - Increment time
  - Check cooldown queue front — if `releaseTime == time` → release back to Max Heap
  - If Max Heap not empty → poll most frequent task, decrement count, if count > 0 put into cooldown queue with `releaseTime = time + n + 1`
  - If Max Heap empty → CPU idles, time increments naturally
- Continue until both Max Heap and cooldown queue are empty
- Return time

**Why releaseTime = time + n + 1:**
- Task used at time=1, cooldown=2
- Cannot use at time=2 and time=3
- Available again at time=4 = 1+2+1

**TC:** O(totalIntervals) where totalIntervals can be O(tasks.length × n) in worst case

**SC:** O(1) since unique tasks are at most 26
// Brute Force — Simulation approach
// TC → O(totalIntervals) where totalIntervals can be O(tasks.length * n)
// SC → O(1) since unique tasks <= 26
class Solution {
    public int leastInterval(char[] tasks, int n) {
        Map<Character, Integer> hm = new HashMap<>();
        for(char c: tasks) {
            hm.put(c, hm.getOrDefault(c, 0) + 1);
        }

        PriorityQueue<Integer> mHeap = new PriorityQueue<>(Comparator.reverseOrder());
        for(int count: hm.values()) {
            mHeap.offer(count);
        }

        Queue<int[]> cooldownQueue = new LinkedList<>();
        int time = 0;

        while(!mHeap.isEmpty() || !cooldownQueue.isEmpty()) {
            time++;

            // release from cooldown first
            if(!cooldownQueue.isEmpty() && time == cooldownQueue.peek()[1]) {
                mHeap.offer(cooldownQueue.poll()[0]);
            }

            // execute task or idle
            if(!mHeap.isEmpty()) {
                int count = mHeap.poll() - 1;
                if(count > 0) {
                    cooldownQueue.offer(new int[]{count, time + n + 1});
                }
            }
        }
        return time;
    }
}
